  "description": "Historical view of which checks alerted (pushed DOWN to Uptime-Kuma) and when, reconstructed from Loki (31-day retention). Kuma itself keeps only current state; this is the history. TWO alert paths are read, because monitor-bridge polls no Kuma state and so logs nothing about the crons that push Kuma themselves: query A is monitor-bridge's container log, query B is `{job=\"syslog\"} |= \"status=down\"` from the host crons (longhorn-backup-health, manifest-prune-check, claude-otel-health). NOT covered: secret-rotation-audit and live-drift-check emit no `status=` token, so they are invisible to B until their scripts log one. CLI equivalent: `uv run python scripts/diagnostics/probe.py alerts`.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "bf4q19tuivta8e"
      },
      "description": "How many cycles each check spent DOWN over the dashboard's time range. A cycle is one evaluation (~5 min for monitor-bridge, the cron's own period for a host cron), so this is firing *duration*, not distinct incidents. Two queries because two alert paths exist: A reads monitor-bridge's container log, B reads the host crons that push Kuma directly and log through `logger` \u2014 monitor-bridge polls no Kuma state, so its log carries nothing about them.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "continuous-GrYlRd"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": false
        },
        "maxVizHeight": 300,
        "minVizHeight": 16,
        "minVizWidth": 8,
        "namePlacement": "auto",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "sizing": "auto",
        "valueMode": "color"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.3.1",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "bf4q19tuivta8e"
          },
          "direction": "backward",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (name) (count_over_time({container=\"monitor-bridge\"} |= \"DOWN\" |~ \"$check\" | pattern `[<_>] DOWN <name> -<_>` [$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "bf4q19tuivta8e"
          },
          "direction": "backward",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (name) (count_over_time({job=\"syslog\"} |= \"status=down\" |~ \"$check\" | regexp `^\\S+ \\S+ (?P<name>[\\w.-]+):` [$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "DOWN cycles by check (range total)",
      "type": "bargauge"
